<title>NETHERLANDS: Aegon details stock dividend.</title>
<headline>Aegon details stock dividend.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1996-09-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Insurer Aegon said on Thursday it had set its 1996 interim optional stock dividend at one new share per 73 held.</p>
<p>&quot;The value of the interim dividend in shares is therefore 3.85 percent lower than the cash dividend,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>On August 22 Aegon announced it would pay an interim cash dividend of 1.18 guilders per common share, up from 0.62 guilders last year.</p>
<p>The increase reflects a change in the method of payment, as interim pay-outs have been hiked to half of the previous year's full-year dividend.</p>
<p>Aegon shares closed at 84.00 guilders on the Amsterdam Stock Exchange on Wednesday, down 0.50 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
